course: dictionary
lesson: 6540
title: Never and its many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Never» means not at any time, not even once. Read this rule: «Never go into old mines, caves or tunnels.» It tells you not to go there, ever, because they can collapse.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in «not ever». In the sentence «The black box helps investigators find out why, so that it never happens again», the clue word «again» tells you the thing does not happen a second time. Try «not ever» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Never» can also be a strong «no» or a surprise. «He ate 12 pies? Never!» does not mean he never ate anything. It means I can't believe it. Read the whole sentence before you decide what the word means.
fact: Never means not at any time, not even once.
fact: «Never ever» is a stronger way to say never, and «never mind» means do not worry about it.
fact: In casual UK and Irish talk, «Never!» means I can't believe it.
fact: The stiff, formal forms are «at no time», «on no occasion» and «under no circumstances».
fact: Context clues such as «again», «ever» or «every winter» can help you work out which meaning of never the author wants.
exercise: «Never carry packages or bags for strangers.» What does never mean here? | Only when you feel like it | *Not at any time, not even once | Quickly and carefully | Often, every single day
exercise: The advice is «never to go onto ice on ponds, lakes, rivers or canals.» What is the advice? | Go onto the ice only on Sundays | *Do not go onto the ice, at any time | Stand near the edge to look | Skate on the ice with your friends
exercise: «He ate 12 pies? Never!» What does «Never!» mean here? | I will eat more pies | Please stop eating now | *I can't believe it | Not at any time
test: What happens to the kernel if pollen «never» lands on the silk? | It grows only in winter | It grows a little more each day | *It never grows | It grows very big
test: «Never mind, you can try again.» What does «never mind» mean? | Mind the step | *Do not worry about it | Remember this forever | I cannot hear you
exam: «Under no circumstances may the door be left open.» What does «under no circumstances» mean? | Very carefully indeed | With the door wide open | *In no situation at all, never | Only on Tuesdays
